<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ismail II of Granada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1339">1339</a>–<a href="/years/1360">1360</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ismail II was Nasrid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> from August 1359 to June 1360. He came to power in a palace coup that deposed his half-brother Muhammad V, but within a year he was overthrown and killed by his kinsman and former supporter, who took the throne as Muhammad VI. His brief reign was part of the dynastic instability that repeatedly weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a>.</p></div>
